The electromagnetic efficiency of the baseline AF-PMSM was evaluated through a segmented loss analysis, where the total power dissipation (P total ) was derived by aggregating the iron core, armature copper, permanent magnet, and mechanical loss components. The computational framework and resulting power balance are discussed below. Equation  6 , which shows the total iron core loss (P core ) for the M19_24G silicon steel stator was computed using the Bertotti separation principle [ 155 ]. This method was selected over standard Steinmetz equations to accurately account for the harmonic-rich flux waveforms inherent in axial flux topologies. The total iron core loss is expressed as the summation of hysteresis (K h ), eddy current (K c ), and excess (K e ) components. 6 \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
